```
To determine the energy required to launch a rocket into space, we would need to know the mass of the rocket and the velocity it needs to achieve to escape Earth's gravity. Let's say the mass of the rocket is 100,000 kg and the velocity it needs to achieve is 11,186 m/s (the escape velocity of Earth). Using the kinetic energy formula above, we can calculate the energy required:
```cpp
