PHP is a server-side scripting language that is commonly used for web development. While it is possible to use PHP for text analysis and visualization, it is not the most suitable language for this task. Tools such as Python and R are more commonly used for text analysis and visualization.
That being said, it is possible to use PHP to perform some basic text analysis tasks such as counting the frequency of words in a text and generating word clouds. Here is an example code for counting the frequency of words in a text:
```php
<?php
// Read the text file into a string
$text = file_get_contents('to_kill_a_mockingbird.txt');
// Convert the text to lowercase
$text = strtolower($text);
// Remove all non-alphanumeric characters
$text = preg_replace('/[^a-z0-9 ]/', '', $text);
// Split the text into words
$words = explode(' ', $text);
// Count the frequency of each word
$word_counts = array_count_values($words);
// Sort the words by frequency in descending order
arsort($word_counts);
// Print the top 10 most frequent words
$i = 0;
foreach ($word_counts as $word => $count) {
  echo "$word: $count\n";
  $i++;
  if ($i == 10) {
    break;
  }
}
?>
```
This code reads the text file "to_kill_a_mockingbird.txt" into a string, converts the text to lowercase, removes all non-alphanumeric characters, splits the text into words, counts the frequency of each word, and prints the top 10 most frequent words.
