How can I implement a program in C++ to redact personal information such as names and addresses from a given passage, while maintaining the original meaning of the text, and ensuring that the redacted information is stored in a separate file for audit purposes? 
Here is the passage I need to redact: 
John Smith is a software engineer at the ABC Company. His office address is 8 Main Street, Anytown.
[C++ code]
```c++
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <regex>
#include <fstream>
using namespace std;
int main() {
    string passage = "John Smith is a software engineer at the ABC Company. His office address is 8 Main Street, Anytown.";
    regex name_regex("(\\b[A-Z][a-z]*\\b\\s*)+");
    regex address_regex("\\d+\\s+([a-zA-Z]+|[a-zA-Z]+\\s[a-zA-Z]+)\\s+(St.|Street|Ave.|Avenue|Blvd.|Boulevard|Dr.|Drive)");
    ofstream audit_file;
    audit_file.open("redacted_info.txt");
    audit_file << "Redacted Names: " << regex_replace(passage, name_regex, "[REDACTED]") << endl;
    audit_file << "Redacted Addresses: " << regex_replace(passage, address_regex, "[REDACTED]") << endl;
    audit_file.close();
    return 0;
}
```
This program uses regular expressions to match and redact names and addresses from the given passage, while keeping the original text intact, and stores the redacted information in a separate file for audit purposes.

