    regex name_regex("(\\b[A-Z][a-z]*\\b\\s*)+");
    regex address_regex("\\d+\\s+([a-zA-Z]+|[a-zA-Z]+\\s[a-zA-Z]+)\\s+(St.|Street|Ave.|Avenue|Blvd.|Boulevard|Dr.|Drive)");
    string line;
    while (getline(in, line)) {
        out << regex_replace(line, name_regex, "[REDACTED]") << endl;
        out << regex_replace(line, address_regex, "[REDACTED]") << endl;
    }
    in.close();
    out.close();
    return 0;
}
```
This program takes two command-line arguments: the input file name and the output file name. It reads the input file line by line, redacts names and addresses using regular expressions, and writes the redacted lines to the output file. It also handles errors when opening or creating files.

