How can you use JavaScript to validate and clean a large data set? Please provide step-by-step instructions.
Assuming you have the data set in an array, here's one way to validate and clean the data:
1. Define a validation function that takes a record as an argument and returns true if the record is valid, and false otherwise. For example:
function validateRecord(record) {
  // Check that the record has all required fields
  if (!record.id || !record.name || !record.email) {
    return false;
  }
  // Check that the email address is valid
  if (!isValidEmail(record.email)) {
    return false;
  }
  // Check that the id is unique
  if (idExists(record.id)) {
    return false;
  }
  return true;
}
2. Define a cleaning function that takes a record as an argument and returns a cleaned version of the record. For example:
function cleanRecord(record) {
  // Remove any leading/trailing whitespace from string fields
  record.name = record.name.trim();
  record.email = record.email.trim();
  // Convert id to a number
  record.id = parseInt(record.id);
  return record;
}
3. Iterate over the data set and validate each record. If a record is invalid, remove it from the array. For example:
for (var i = data.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
  var record = data[i];
  if (!validateRecord(record)) {
    data.splice(i, 1);
  }
}
4. Iterate over the data set again and clean each record. For example:
for (var i = 0; i < data.length; i++) {
  data[i] = cleanRecord(data[i]);
}
5. Optionally, sort the data set by a specific field using Array.sort(). For example:
data.sort(function(a, b) {
  if (a.name < b.name) {
    return -1;
  } else if (a.name > b.name) {
    return 1;
  } else {
    return 0;
  }
});
This process can be adapted to work with different data models or schemas, such as JSON or SQL databases.

